  "gaps": [
    "The capture says only \"credits\" and never names the credit unit. Semester credits are assumed and have not been verified from the capture.",
    "Residency rules apply to the whole degree, not to specific courses: at least 30 credits (normally the final 30) at UMGC, half the major credits at UMGC, and at least 15 upper-level credits (300–499) at UMGC. The capture does not say which specific requirements must be taken at UMGC, so no item is marked institutionalOnly.",
    "The capture does not list every acceptable course for the 'or any SPCH/COMM/upper-level JOUR/COMM/SPCH course' options. It names only the disciplines.",
    "The ledger does not record the timing and grade conditions on general education. WRTG 112 must be earned with a grade of C- or better within the first 24 credits. Mathematics must be completed within the first 24 credits. The professional exploration course must be taken within the first 6 credits.",
    "The capture lists major courses that may also fit general education (for example JOUR 201 and COMM 390 within Communications). However, no course may count toward both general education and the major, so these are listed once, under the major.",
    "These requirements apply only to students who began continuous enrollment on or after August 1, 2026. The individual student's catalog year is not stated in the capture."
  ],
